    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "凡从人间挑选的大祭司，是奉派替人办理属　神的事，为要献上礼物和赎罪祭（或译：要为罪献上礼物和祭物）。",
      "en": "For every high priest is taken from among the people[NOTE:1] and appointed[NOTE:2] to represent them before God,[NOTE:3] to offer both gifts and sacrifices for sins.",
      "notes": [
        "Grk “from among men,” but since the point in context is shared humanity (rather than shared maleness), the plural Greek term ἀνθρώπων (anthrōpōn) has been translated “people.”",
        "Grk “who is taken from among people is appointed.”",
        "Grk “appointed on behalf of people in reference to things relating to God.”"
      ],
